Minato's patch to frameworks/base's rs/java/android/renderscript/RenderScript.java at android-15.0.0_r1
(Apache-2.0), the Unity test APK gap sort's category 2: RenderScript.create throws RSRuntimeException, a named departure.

Why: Android 15 still runs RenderScript on its CPU driver (libRS with libRSCpuRef, through librs_jni), and Minato
builds neither, so the static init would fail to load rs_jni and throw RSRuntimeException out of <clinit>: an app
gets ExceptionInInitializerError, which no catch of RSRuntimeException takes, and every later use of the class
NoClassDefFoundError. The off switch config.disable_renderscript has create() return null instead, and an app then
crashes with a NullPointerException. So the static init loads nothing, and every create (through internalCreate)
logs once through Unwritten and throws RSRuntimeException, which blur libraries and apps catch before they fall back
to Java. Code that does not catch it still breaks, where it works on Android. So does RenderScriptGL's constructor,
which makes its device through nDeviceCreate, not internalCreate (webview-camera-test, ADR-0058 d)).

